findings.required_change:
Have the generator write:
- broker statements (cash and held units) for the accounts;
- trades on some openings, and saved groups whose members span uncoupled instruments;
- revisions that change a row's instrument, account, quantity or kind, and that add or remove `leg-unstated` (both with and without an instrument);
- an adjustment arriving or changing without its record;
- a change to an instrument (terms) and to an account (managed) alone.
Keep the full-engine comparisons on every step.

items.evidence:
The comparison part is done. `Engine::match_disagrees` (engine.rs:979-1013) compares `Matched` whole, field by field (trips, books, beyond, dust, arrived, last_price, stock_dividends, disagreements, unit_disagreements, unapplied, units, roles, waiting, cash), then `Identity`, families, symbols and cash shares. by_change.rs:246-249 also asserts `e.figures().matched == &match_lots(&now)`.

The generator part is only partly done (by_change.rs:45-153). It does write:
- a leg-unstated row naming no instrument (case 11);
- a multi-leg record on uncoupled X and V at one day, beside a sale of each (case 12);
- an event whose parent W is not the anchor's instrument (case 10, 10b);
- a coin sent as K and received as K2 (case 9, 10c).

It does not write any of the following:
- `brokers` statements, so `checks` is always empty;
- `trades`, so `Identity` holds only `needs_trade`, and `trade_of`, `moved`, `joined` and `unclaimed` are never filled;
- `groups`;
- successions, which the engine has no input for (a join or a part would show as a revision moving a transaction's instrument).

Revisions only add 1 to cash (by_change.rs:221-227: `t.cash = t.cash.map(|c| ... checked_add(Dec::ONE) ...)`). A transaction never moves family, account, problems or link on revision, and a revision of a row with no cash (transfers, events, expiries) changes nothing. There is also no leg-unstated row that names an instrument, and no change to an instrument or account alone.
